From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:54:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: thunderbolt: apple,t8103-usb4-acio: add
 the router's CIO PHY

On the J713 a deep sleep powers the USB4 host router off with its
Type-C PHY, and the router's host takes the PHY through the sleep with
it. Let the router name that PHY.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6ec513fdd62cef9a64c7dc197738b6f094e43961)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-acio.yaml    | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-acio.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-acio.yaml
index 9f6f992410..562fb2f315 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-acio.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thunderbolt/apple,t8103-usb4-acio.yaml
@@ -119,6 +119,16 @@ properties:
     description:
       GPIO on the pin that carries the router's LSTX sideband signal.
 
+  phys:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      The Type-C PHY whose lanes carry the router's CIO link. A host that
+      power-cycles the router for a deep sleep takes the PHY through the
+      sleep with it.
+
+  phy-names:
+    const: cio
+
   apple,pcie-tunnel:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
     description:
-- 
